-- Plan section 3B: the existing fatal versus source-declared Error! integrity routes, including
-- synthetic start. A fallible external float whose successful payload is non-finite is a fatal
-- integrity guard in the synthetic entry: the legally placed catch below recovers declared errors,
-- not the guard, so page execution stops with no output. The binary64 destination delivers the
-- NaN unchanged, so this is a directly delivered raw non-finite value rather than a rounded
-- overflow. The run halts, so the case asserts the outcome category and the absence of any
-- fallback output instead of pinning the guard message text.
@nan_float.js fallible_nan

code ~U32 = 0
value = fallible_nan() catch |err|:
    code = err.code
    then 0.0
;
io.line([: external_native_float64_start_nonfinite code=[code]])
